{"kind":"symbol","primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"platforms":["macOS"],"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"at"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"_"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"internalParam","text":"time"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:11GnustoClock9TimeOfDayV","identifier":"doc:\/\/GnustoClock\/documentation\/GnustoClock\/TimeOfDay","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"TimeOfDay"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"named"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"internalParam","text":"name"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:SS","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"String"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"perform"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"internalParam","text":"body"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"attribute","text":"@escaping "},{"kind":"attribute","text":"@Sendable"},{"kind":"text","text":" () "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"throws"},{"kind":"text","text":" -> "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:s4Voida","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Void"},{"kind":"text","text":") -> "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:6Gnusto10TimedEventV","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/TimedEvent","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"TimedEvent"}]}]},{"parameters":[{"name":"time","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"When it goes off."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"name":"name","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The daemon’s name, unique across the whole game."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"name":"body","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"What happens."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"kind":"parameters"},{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"anchor":"return-value","type":"heading","text":"Return Value"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The timed event, for the game’s "},{"code":"timers","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" block."}]}]},{"content":[{"level":2,"anchor":"discussion","type":"heading","text":"Discussion"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The alarm fires ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"once","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":", at the end of the first turn on or after its","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"time — so a clock running several minutes per turn that steps over the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"target still fires, and so does one the host jumps forward by hand. A","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"time earlier in the day than the clock’s start means ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"tomorrow","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":", which"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"is what an overnight game wants.","type":"text"}]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Firing once is enforced by the alarm stopping its own daemon, so the"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"arming state is ordinary daemon state: it saves and restores for free,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"stopDaemon(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" cancels an alarm that hasn’t fired, and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"startDaemon(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" re-arms one that has."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Timer names are global across a game, so prefix yours — the clock’s own"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"convention is "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"\"clock.<something>\""},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/gnustoclock\/clock\/at(_:named:perform:)"]}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/GnustoClock\/documentation\/GnustoClock\/Clock\/at(_:named:perform:)"},"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"m